Run the java that shutil.which() finds.

PyGhidraLauncher.java_home checks for java on the PATH with
shutil.which() but then runs the bare name. On Windows which() also
matches java.cmd and java.bat through PATHEXT, while CreateProcess
looks only for java.exe, so a PATH whose java is a .cmd, as MSYS2's
openjdk installs, ends in an uncaught FileNotFoundError, and a java.exe
from a later PATH entry runs instead when there is one. Running the
path which() returned makes the check and LaunchSupport use the java
it found.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/src/pyghidra/launcher.py
+++ b/src/pyghidra/launcher.py
@@ -320,8 +320,8 @@
             # Check to see if java is on the PATH. If not, use JAVA_HOME.
             # NOTE: shutils.which() is not enough...macOS puts a stub java on the PATH which
             # will prevent that from working as expected, so you have to actually run it.
-            java_cmd = 'java'
-            if not shutil.which(java_cmd) or subprocess.run([java_cmd, "-version"], stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL).returncode != 0:
+            java_cmd = shutil.which('java')
+            if not java_cmd or subprocess.run([java_cmd, "-version"], stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL).returncode != 0:
                 java_home_dir = os.environ.get('JAVA_HOME')
                 if java_home_dir and os.path.isdir(java_home_dir):
                     java_cmd = java_home_dir + "/bin/java"
